INT. OPEN-PLAN OFFICE, BEANBAG ZONE - DAY

A startup floor painted in primary colors. Ping-pong table. A neon sign reads: WE'RE A FAMILY. Three beanbag chairs in a triangle around a kombucha tap.

CASSIDY ROWE-ADEYEMI (30s, product manager, hoodie) and BARNABY OKONJO-LIND (30s, engineer, noise-canceling headphones around his neck) sit in beanbags. DESMOND "DEZ" HARTWELL (40s, Head of Culture, ironic vest) stands, clapping slowly.

DEZ
Team! Quick one! Pulse check!

CASSIDY
No.

BARNABY
Not now.

DEZ
Just a quick pulse check on how we're all feeling about the pivot!

Cassidy flicks her eyes to Barnaby. Barnaby lifts his headphones to his ears and drops them back on his neck. Dez keeps clapping.

CASSIDY
Dez, we pivoted in March.

DEZ
Right!

CASSIDY
We pivoted again in June.

DEZ
Right!

BARNABY
We're pivoting back, aren't we.

DEZ
(too quickly)
I can't speak to that.

BARNABY
You just did.

Dez stops clapping. Cassidy grabs the nearest cup of kombucha and drinks it in one pull. Barnaby wriggles upright in his beanbag, which swallows him again. Dez lunges to help, steps on a cable, and the ping-pong table's overhead lamp swings. They all duck.

A woman in a tailored suit appears at the edge of the zone, a tablet cradled in one arm: VERONIKA SANDOVAL-BRIGHT (50s, investor, pearl studs, silver hair, no smile).

VERONIKA
Is this a bad time?

DEZ
(too bright)
Veronika! We were just aligning!

VERONIKA
On what?

DEZ
Vision!

VERONIKA
Whose?

Nobody speaks. Cassidy and Barnaby look at their shoes. Dez adjusts his vest.

BARNABY
(muttering)
Oh, boy.

VERONIKA
I've reviewed the burn rate. We have six weeks of runway.

DEZ
That's actually a positive!

VERONIKA
It is not a positive.

CASSIDY
Veronika, if I may.

VERONIKA
You may.

CASSIDY
We've been building the wrong thing since March.

Dez gasps. Barnaby stares at her. Veronika's eyebrows rise a quarter inch.

VERONIKA
Explain.

CASSIDY
We pivoted to chase a market, but the customers wanted the original product. We never listened.

DEZ
Cass.

CASSIDY
It's true, Dez.

BARNABY
It is true.

VERONIKA
Then why did no one say so?

Dez opens his mouth, closes it, sits down in the third beanbag, and disappears into it up to his chest. The neon sign buzzes over his head.

DEZ
(small)
We're a family.

VERONIKA
Families go bankrupt, Desmond.

She taps her tablet. Then, to her own faint surprise, she lowers herself into the arm of Cassidy's beanbag and sets the tablet on her knee.

VERONIKA (CONT'D)
Start from March.
